$ A CBUSH (CID 0) between coincident grids, the first fixed and a load on the second in basic:
$ FORCE 100 along (.3, .5, .8) and MOMENT 10 along (.6, 0, .8). The BUSH engineering forces must equal the load,
$ (30, 50, 80, 6, 0, 8), whatever the grids' output (CD) systems. Here both grids are in the rotated CD 5; the
$ transform of the node forces to basic used one component three times, giving (13.7, 25.5, 39.0, 2.5, -5.8, 3.5).
SOL 101
CEND
TITLE = CBUSH FORCES WITH ROTATED GRID OUTPUT SYSTEMS
LOAD = 1
DISPLACEMENT = ALL
FORCE = ALL
BEGIN BULK
CORD2R,5,,0.,0.,0.,.2,.3,.9,+C5
+C5,1.,.4,.1
GRID,1,,0.,0.,0.,5,123456
GRID,2,,0.,0.,0.,5
CBUSH,10,20,1,2,,,,0
PBUSH,20,K,1.E4,2.E4,3.E4,4.E4,5.E4,6.E4
FORCE,1,2,0,100.,.3,.5,.8
MOMENT,1,2,0,10.,.6,.0,.8
ENDDATA
